The project info line is a consistent way to display a project wherever it is listed as one item among others.

## Overview

<%= embed OpenProject::Projects::InfoLineComponentPreview, :playground %>

## Anatomy

The info line consists of:

- Project name, linking to the project unless it is archived
- Workspace type (optional): icon and name of the workspace type (Portfolio, Program, Project)
- Archived label, shown only for archived projects

Only the project name is interactive. All other interaction has to come from the element using this component.

## Used in

- Projects tab of a work package type

### Code structure

```ruby
render(Projects::InfoLineComponent.new(project: @project))
render(Projects::InfoLineComponent.new(project: @project, show_workspace_type: true))
```
